{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790261147,"nonce":"BqSqXslHuwccvbqOFQJtbZQmQ54=","title":"Inliner: counting only a callee's hot blocks grows deltablue's compile time","message":"With calls and size counted off a callee's cold paths (commit 4c42cdd5, git-bug 4e3f96c), callees whose error arms carry calls stop being call-bearing and are inlined at sites outside loops, and more call-bearing callees fit the 48-instruction cap at loop sites. On speed/deltablue --fast that raises inlined sites from about 197 to about 271, the optimised bodies from 7617 to about 9400 instructions (chain_test 425 to 988, Planner.remove_propagate_from 304 to 675, projection_test 899 to 1139), and the summed optimisation passes from about 133 to 168 ms (NUC, ZYNTAX_TRACE_OPT_PHASES=1, 7 interleaved runs). The inline pass itself goes from about 18 to 32 ms. deltablue's first iteration rises from about 130 to 158-174 ms and its mean from 28.5 to 34-38 ms in the speed harness; richards, go, binary_trees and records move within noise.\n\nA variant keeping Malloc/Free as calls showed the same growth (265 inlines), so the cold-path rule, not the constructor rule, is the cause.\n\nOptions: charge a callee's cold blocks at sites outside loops (they are copied there even if they never run), outline cold arms before inlining so a site copies only the hot path, or cap the growth of a function that runs once (git-bug 981e482).","files":null}]}